<p>President Trump said the United States would begin a naval blockade focused on ships entering or leaving Iranian ports after 21 hours of US-Iran talks in Islamabad ended without a deal to end the war. US Central Command later described a narrower operation than Trump’s initial language suggested, saying the blockade would apply to maritime traffic entering or leaving Iranian ports and coastal areas, while vessels transiting the Strait of Hormuz to and from non-Iranian ports would not be impeded. The talks broke down over two main sticking points that several outlets highlighted: reopening the strait and Iran’s nuclear program, including uranium stockpiles. Markets reacted quickly. Oil rose above $100 a barrel and equities fell as traders weighed the risk of a deeper energy shock and renewed fighting. Even so, there is still some room for de-escalation: Pakistan said it would keep facilitating dialogue, and several reports noted that the operational order stops short of closing the waterway to non-Iranian shipping.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/hX4d7jZupCAimqUvvqbiYkdZKMlToVlVr1FsdWpWS6TlIR1qB6VL_JTvxoTuON7Tid548A0K-VjRjz2b_1RDFiW-nXRKM0C6bP8xt4zyRH1n' alt='Cargo ships in the Gulf, near the Strait of Hormuz, as seen from northern Ras al-Khaimah.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Start time: CENTCOM said enforcement would begin at 1400 GMT on April 13, or 10 a.m. Eastern Time, giving the operation a clear start time rather than leaving it as an open-ended announcement.</li><li>Shipping response: Shipping data showed oil tankers steering clear of Hormuz ahead of the blockade, while ships carrying Iranian oil were reported anchored off India as companies assessed the new risks.</li><li>Retaliation risk: Iran’s Revolutionary Guards said they would treat any military vessels approaching the strait as a ceasefire breach and warned they would respond forcefully.</li><li>Allied stance: The UK ruled out joining the operation, while Australia said it had not been asked to participate and did not expect to be.</li><li>Asia exposure: Analysts cited by regional outlets warned that the disruption could hit Asian importers, and China in particular, especially hard, with one worst-case estimate putting oil near $170 a barrel.</li></ul><blockquote>The blockade will be enforced impartially against vessels of all nations entering or departing Iranian ports and coastal areas, including all Iranian ports on the Arabian Gulf and Gulf of Oman. - US Central Command</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US Central Command: CENTCOM described the plan as a targeted maritime operation covering Iranian ports while preserving freedom of navigation for ships using non-Iranian ports. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/12/world/iran-war-trump-talks-pakistan'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Iranian Revolutionary Guards Corps: The IRGC said the strait remains open to non-military vessels under Iranian rules but warned that military vessels approaching it would be considered in violation of the ceasefire. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1991096/after-trumps-blockade-announcement-irgc-says-will-view-military-vessels-approaching-hormuz-as-ceasefire-breach'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Pakistan: Pakistan said it would keep facilitating dialogue and urged both sides to honor the fragile two-week ceasefire despite the failed talks. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1991295/us-military-to-begin-blockade-of-iranian-ports-on-monday'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>United Kingdom: British officials ruled out taking part in a key strait operation, a sign of caution among US partners about widening the conflict at sea. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/55e4467b-19c3-433e-851c-2966f60c9f84'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>Australia: Prime Minister Anthony Albanese said Australia had not been asked to help and did not expect to be, signaling that Canberra would stay out of the naval effort. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/australia-wont-join-trumps-strait-of-hormuz-blockade/'>Michael West</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-trump-orders-hormuz-blockade-after-us-iran-peace-talks-end-with-no/'>Trump orders Hormuz blockade after US-Iran peace talks end with no agreement</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/iran-protests-live-blog-trump-khamenei/33640284.html'>Trump Confirms Blockade Of Iranian Ports</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/4dbf076f-004b-4244-8579-2aca3e60e05c'>Oil prices soar above $100 a barrel as hope fades of end to Iran war</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-iran-war-news-why-donald-trump-wants-to-block-strait-of-hormuz-already-in-irans-grip-how-will-it-work-11349440#publisher=newsstand'>Trump Says US Will Block The Already Blocked Hormuz. How It Will Work</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/ships-with-iran-oil-anchor-off-india-as-trump-announces-blockade'>Ships with Iran oil anchor off India as Trump announces blockade</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/4/13/oil-prices-surge-past-103-a-barrel-after-us-announces-blockade-of-iran'>Oil prices surge past $103 a barrel after US announces blockade of Iran</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/australia-wont-join-trumps-strait-of-hormuz-blockade/'>Australia won’t join Trump’s Strait of Hormuz blockade</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/12/2026/donald-trump-says-the-us-will-blockade-hormuz'>Donald Trump says the US will ‘blockade’ Hormuz</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cn781z4lgg4o'>Oil back above $100 as US to blockade Iranian ports after peace talks fail</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/638259-us-iran-oil-blockade/'>Trump mulls new ‘limited strikes’ on Iran as looming naval blockade sends oil above $100: LIVE UPDAT